  "main_text": "News & Events\nNews & Analysis\nLatest News\nLatest News\n\nNews, announcements, and analysis from the CHERI Alliance and its members.\n\nNews and analysis\n\nThe complete Alliance news archive, ordered with the newest article first.\n\n29 July 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nA new ETSI standard could rewrite the memory-safety debate\n\nMike Eftimakis – CHERI Alliance ETSI TS 104 198 establishes a common language for memory safety Memory-safety vulnerabilities remain one of the largest sources of critical software vulner...\n\nRead article\n\n15 July 2026\nEcosystem\n\nThe leading Root-of-Trust now integrates CHERI security technology\n\nAdam Finney – CHERI Alliance If you are building secure hardware, the way you protect software running inside that hardware matters just as much as the cryptography around it. That is why...\n\nRead article\n\n17 June 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nCombatting the AI threat with CHERI\n\nIn 2025 alone, global cybercrime costs reached an estimated $1.2 billion every minute, with projections rising to $1.8 billion per minute by 2029. Just seven years earlier, the figure was...\n\nRead article\n\n13 May 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nIntroducing the CHERI Adoption Global Ecosystem Assessment Q1 2026\n\nIn 2025 alone, global cybercrime costs reached an estimated $1.2 billion every minute, with projections rising to $1.8 billion per minute by 2029. Just seven years earlier, the figure was...\n\nRead article\n\n4 May 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nOne Bug is All It Takes\n\nIn 2025 alone, global cybercrime costs reached an estimated $1.2 billion every minute, with projections rising to $1.8 billion per minute by 2029. Just seven years earlier, the figure was...\n\nRead article\n\n29 April 2026\nEcosystem\n\nWhy Codasip went all‑in on CHERI\n\nInterview with Ron Black, CEO of Codasip Codasip is a founding member of the CHERI Alliance and one of the most active industrial players in the CHERI ecosystem. From the outset, Codasip ...\n\nRead article\n\n28 April 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nCHERI memory safety mitigates LLM-discovered vulnerability in FreeBSD\n\nBrooks Davis – Capabilities Limited This article is part of a series of blogs published after the announcement of Mythos vulnerabilities’ exploitation capabilities. The views from other e...\n\nRead article\n\n21 April 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nWind River Joins the CHERI Alliance\n\nWe are pleased to welcome Wind River to the CHERI Alliance, marking another important step forward in building a more secure computing ecosystem. Building on its existing work with CHERI,...\n\nRead article\n\n14 April 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nAI has compressed the attack timeline\n\nMike Eftimakis – CHERI Alliance This article is part of a series of blogs published after the announcement of Mythos vulnerabilities’ exploitation capabilities. The views from other exper...\n\nRead article\n\n16 March 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nICENI: First Look\n\nFor more than a decade, CHERI research has demonstrated that hardware enforced memory safety can eliminate entire classes of security vulnerabilities. Much of this work has taken place in...\n\nRead article\n\n19 February 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nThe Capable Hub joins the CHERI Alliance to accelerate cybersecurity collaboration\n\nStrengthening the CHERI ecosystem through Open-Source innovation We are excited to announce that The Capable Hub has become a member of the CHERI Alliance, a significant step forward in o...\n\nRead article\n\n4 February 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nThe EU Cyber Resilience Act: What It Means for Secure-by-Design Systems and CHERI\n\nIn 2025 alone, global cybercrime costs reached an estimated $1.2 billion every minute, with projections rising to $1.8 billion per minute by 2029. Just seven years earlier, the figure was...\n\nRead article\n\n3 February 2026\nCHERI Alliance news\n\nAmid rising cyber threats, EnSilica joins the CHERI Alliance to enable safe & secure silicon\n\nOxford UK